The '''2000 UEFA Cup final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match that took place on 17 May 2000 at [[Telia Parken|Parken Stadium]] in Copenhagen, Denmark to decide the winner of the [[1999–2000 UEFA Cup]]. The game event pitted [[Galatasaray S.K. (football)|Galatasaray]] of Turkey and [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] of England, and was the final match of the 1999–2000 season, the 29th final of Europe's second largest club football competition, the [[UEFA Europa League|UEFA Cup]]. It was Galatasaray's first appearance in a final of a European tournament and Arsenal's first UEFA Cup final.

Both clubs competed in the [[1999–2000 UEFA Champions League]] first group stage, with each team finishing in third place; Galatasaray behind [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] and [[Hertha BSC]] and Arsenal behind [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] and [[ACF Fiorentina|Fiorentina]], thus exiting the competition, and qualifying for the third round of the UEFA Cup. From there, the two sides advanced through the fourth round, the quarter-finals and the semi-finals to progress to the final. Galatasaray overcame [[Bologna FC 1909|Bologna]], [[Borussia Dortmund]], [[RCD Mallorca|Mallorca]] and [[Leeds United F.C.|Leeds United]] on their way, while Arsenal defeated [[FC Nantes|Nantes]], [[Deportivo de La Coruña|Deportivo La Coruña]], [[SV Werder Bremen|Werder Bremen]] and [[RC Lens|Lens]].

The match was attended by 38,919 spectators, as Galatasaray won 4–1 on penalties following extra time, making it the first time for a Turkish side to win a European honour. They also obtained a [[Treble (association football)|Treble]], having also won the Turkish league championship and the Turkish domestic cup titles. As a result of their triumph, Galatasaray became the first UEFA Cup winner to compete for the [[UEFA Super Cup]], following the dissolution of the [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]], and also initially qualified for the later-cancelled [[2001 FIFA Club World Championship]]. The final was marred by the [[2000 UEFA Cup final riots|riots between supporters of the two sides]].

